.\" merisio(1) - Merisio GUI application man page
.TH MERISIO 1 "2026-05-17" "Merisio 1.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
merisio \- a modern MERISE database modeling tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B merisio
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Merisio
is a graphical MERISE database modeling application built with Python and
PySide6. It provides a visual editor for creating and editing Conceptual Data
Models (MCD), viewing the derived Logical Data Model (MLD), and generating
PostgreSQL DDL statements.
.PP
When launched without arguments, the graphical editor opens.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a brief usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B MCD Editor
Visual diagram editor for entities, associations, and links with
drag-and-drop positioning, multi-selection, cardinalities (0,1), (0,N),
(1,1), (1,N), and configurable link styles (curved with Catmull-Rom
smoothing, orthogonal with L-routing, straight).
.TP
.B Link Editing
Select a link to reveal draggable waypoint handles for reshaping the
path, and segment-midpoint handles for inserting new bends. Magnetic
snap during drag with orthogonal segment-axis-lock. Right-click menu
to Remove waypoint, Tidy Up Link (collapse near-collinear waypoints),
or Straighten Link (wipe all). The cardinality label is also
draggable along the link's path.
.TP
.B Undo / Redo
Snapshot-based history covering every modification. Use Ctrl+Z to
undo and Ctrl+Shift+Z to redo. Bounded to the 100 most recent steps.
.TP
.B Data Dictionary
Overview of all attributes across entities.
.TP
.B MLD View
Logical Data Model with auto-generated table/column tree view.
Column names can be renamed by right-clicking or double-clicking.
.TP
.B SQL Generation
PostgreSQL CREATE TABLE statements derived from the MLD.
.TP
.B Diagram Export
Export diagrams to SVG, PNG, or PDF formats via File > Export Diagram.
.TP
.B Diagram Colours
Customisable colours for entities, associations, and links via
Options > Diagram Colours.
.SH FILE FORMAT
Projects are stored as JSON files with the
.B .merisio
extension (format version 2.2). A project file contains metadata, MCD
definitions (entities, associations, links with optional waypoints and
cardinality label positions), MLD column overrides, and colour
settings. Older 2.1 files load with empty waypoints and the default
label position (0.2).
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TS
l l.
Ctrl+N	New Project
Ctrl+O	Open Project
Ctrl+S	Save Project
Ctrl+Shift+S	Save As
Ctrl+Z	Undo
Ctrl+Shift+Z	Redo
Ctrl+B	Toggle Sidebar
Ctrl+J	Toggle Output Panel
Ctrl+1	MCD Tab
Ctrl+2	MLD Tab
F5	Validate Model
Delete	Delete Selected
Ctrl+Scroll	Zoom In/Out
Ctrl++	Zoom In
Ctrl+-	Zoom Out
Ctrl+0	Fit to View
Ctrl+Shift+0	Reset Zoom (100%)
.TE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
